{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/297707-changeling-samhain-question","id":297707,"title":"Changeling Samhain Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-30T19:16:04-07:00","id":297707,"title":"Changeling Samhain Question","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Kinain, those with the fae-blooded merit, and the long-enchanted: are they affected by Samhain?<br /> <br /> My first thoughts are no, but it hits our LARP tomorrow and I want to know if I need to give a heads up to any of those groups *scrounges around more in &quot;Enchanted&quot;*.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T21:53:22-07:00","id":297793,"title":"","content":"&gt;&quot;Enchanted&quot;<br /> <br /> If that's book title, I think you posted in not the right section, since I don't recall Changeling Lost line having book with such title.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T07:49:28-07:00","id":298126,"title":"","content":"I'd say kinain are probably affected by the Samhain Mists just like any kithain. If I were running, I'd probably rule the Samhain Mists even overrule the kinain ability that lets them be immune to the Mists.<br /> <br /> As for the tradition of going Unseelie for the night, a kinain is mortal, so the character wouldn't have an Unseelie legacy to enter. That being said, if a character is already used to eccentricities of the fae, the person probably wouldn't mind joining in on the revelry (depending, of course, on the nature of the revelry and the person in question).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}